Author: Ivy233 <wangjinrun@uniontech.com>
Date: Sat Oct 3 21:40:34 2026 +0800
Subject: fix: skip size request for grabbed drag images

QQuickDragAttachedPrivate::loadPixmap() always passed imageSourceSize()
to QQuickPixmap::load(). When Drag.imageSource holds an itemgrabber URL
(produced by Item::grabToImage()) and no explicit imageSourceSize is
set, the getter falls back to the loader's current size (0x0 for a fresh
loader, or the previous image's size afterwards). QQuickPixmapCache
rightfully warns that a sourceSize request on a grabToImage URL is
ignored, so every drag whose image comes from grabToImage() - the
documented usage pattern - prints a spurious
"Ignoring sourceSize request for image url that came from grabToImage"
warning.

Grabbed images are already fully rendered and are cached under a key
without any size, so the size request is meaningless for them. Only
request a size for non-grabber URLs and when imageSourceSize was
explicitly set.

修复 grabToImage 拖拽图片的 sourceSize 误报：

loadPixmap() 此前无条件把 imageSourceSize() 传给 QQuickPixmap::load()。
当 Drag.imageSource 为 itemgrabber URL（Item::grabToImage() 的结果）且
未显式设置 imageSourceSize 时，回退取 loader 当前尺寸（空 loader 为
0x0，之后为上一张图的尺寸），触发 QQuickPixmapCache 的 "Ignoring
sourceSize request for image url that came from grabToImage" 告警。而
grab 结果已完整渲染且以无尺寸键缓存，尺寸请求对其无意义。现仅对非
grabber URL 请求尺寸。

PMS: TASK-394335
---
Index: qt6-declarative/src/quick/items/qquickdrag.cpp
===================================================================
diff --git qt6-declarative.orig/src/quick/items/qquickdrag.cpp qt6-declarative/src/quick/items/qquickdrag.cpp
index 8095e9b49..7371eab2f 100644
--- qt6-declarative.orig/src/quick/items/qquickdrag.cpp
+++ qt6-declarative/src/quick/items/qquickdrag.cpp
@@ -817,7 +817,16 @@ void QQuickDragAttachedPrivate::loadPixmap()
     const QQmlContext *context = qmlContext(q->parent());
     if (context)
         loadUrl = context->resolvedUrl(imageSource);
-    pixmapLoader.load(context ? context->engine() : nullptr, loadUrl, QRect(), q->imageSourceSize());
+    // A request size is meaningless for itemgrabber URLs (results of
+    // Item::grabToImage()): those images are already fully rendered and are
+    // cached under a size-less key. imageSourceSize() falls back to the size
+    // of the previously loaded image (0x0 for a fresh loader) when no
+    // explicit size was set, which only triggers a spurious "Ignoring
+    // sourceSize request for image url that came from grabToImage" warning
+    // in QQuickPixmapCache. Skip the size request for grabbed images.
+    const bool isGrabbedImage = loadUrl.scheme() == QQuickPixmap::itemGrabberScheme;
+    pixmapLoader.load(context ? context->engine() : nullptr, loadUrl, QRect(),
+                      isGrabbedImage ? QSize() : q->imageSourceSize());
 }
 
 Qt::DropAction QQuickDragAttachedPrivate::startDrag(Qt::DropActions supportedActions)
